		// Mirrors NativeDeleteClothSimulator below. Alice's dress/skirt cloth
		// simulator resolves "the" playable pawn globally and therefore
		// simulates a second Alice's cloth against the first one's bones —
		// the existing fix for that (see MirrorCosmetics) is to delete the
		// native simulator and fall back to plain skinning for the
		// presentation proxy. Hair uses the same native soft-body machinery
		// (Template/PhysicsAsset/Nodes/Strands — see the rotation-candidate
		// tuning code above), so it's a reasonable bet it has the identical
		// "only one Alice" assumption, producing the same kind of
		// structural corruption. This isn't in the generated SDK (the
		// dumper never observed HairComponent.DeleteSimulator being called
		// live), but the params struct for the equivalent cloth function is
		// empty, and UHairComponent.Reset() takes no parameters either — a
		// parameterless DeleteSimulator is a safe, low-risk guess to try,
		// especially since InvokeNativeFunction/FindFunction already fail
		// safely (return false) if this specific function turns out not to
		// exist under this name.
		struct UHairComponent_execDeleteSimulator_Params
		{
		};

